.alert.alert-light.border
  %h3.fw-semibold.mb-2 Goal of this page
  %p.mb-3
    Ensure assignment expectations are aligned. Aligned expectations are how people know how they are doing and where they stand — the foundation for flow and for MAAP to work in an organization.

  %h3.fw-semibold.mb-2 Context
  = render "shared/maap/definition"
  %p.mb-3
    The Expectation Alignment Score (0–100) summarizes whether taking on an assignment is understandable, an appropriate challenge, and relevant, and whether employee and manager check-ins tend to land in the same place. Bands run Strongly Mis-aligned → Strongly Aligned, same as on each assignment’s score card.

  %h3.fw-semibold.mb-2 Specifics of this page
  %h5.fw-semibold.mb-2 What you see
  %ul.mb-3
    %li Spotlight counts non-archived assignments, how many have a score, how many are missing, and how many are stale (calculated more than a day ago).
    %li The distribution chart shows how many assignments fall in each alignment band, plus “No score.”
    %li The 10 best and 10 worst lists link to the assignment page. Use them to celebrate clarity and to find work that needs tightening.
    %li Refresh missing &amp; stale queues background recalculations. Prefer that when many scores are empty or old; use per-row Refresh for a single assignment.

  %h5.fw-semibold.mb-2 Band legend
  %ul.list-unstyled.mb-0
    - AssignmentSurveys::ExpectationAlignmentScore::SCORE_BANDS.each do |band|
      %li.mb-1
        %span.assignment-survey-quality-signal{class: "assignment-survey-quality-#{band[:key]}"}
          %i.bi{class: "#{band[:icon]} me-1"}
          = band[:label]
        %span.text-muted.small
          — #{band[:min]}#{band[:max_exclusive] ? "–#{band[:max_exclusive] - 1}" : "+"}
